{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him","id":1561153,"title":"What on earth does Saulot do in the East, making ALL Wan Kuei hate him","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2026-07-01T01:43:38-07:00","id":1561153,"title":"What on earth does Saulot do in the East, making ALL Wan Kuei hate him","content":"AFAIK:<br /> <br /> He studied under the Xue (the guy who founded the biggest 5 virtue Paths of Wan Kuei), but was proved to be imperfect under the sun and hated, banished from Xue\u2019s company and then returned to the West (KotE, pg. 38)<br /> <br /> He stolen their secrets:<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>Disciplines, he can use it, in an unhealthy way though (KotE, pg. 100), maybe only Dragon Tears (Sunset Empire, pg. 95), but I always think this refers to Obeah/Valern, not original Dragon Tears.</li> <li>Devil-Tigers Dhramas, if you think he is the 3 founders of Baali then he refers to this Dharma to create it (also implying his journey to the east is during 2nd City period)</li> </ol>He left the bloodline Wu Zao to deal with Wan Kuei<br /> <br /> He Embraced a jomon guy later called mokur and greatly pushed the foundation of Inconnu (Lair of the Hidden, pg. 16)<br /> <br /> He has killed many Wan Kuei (Gehenna, pg. 114, it\u2019s from one chronicle so may not be canonical)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24560-rock113","name":"Rock113","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24560_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"720"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T02:43:23-07:00","id":1561154,"title":"","content":"He was, first of all, a &quot;barbarian&quot;<br /> The borders of the Middle Kingdom is a bit malleable, to this day, shifts around a bit ,but back in those days the First City was very close to their borders - a border the Yama Kings set up with their machination accidentaly sealing themselves out fro mthe West and they can't claim any souls of the &quot;primitive barbarians&quot; but they not really considered it a loss<br /> In the eyes of the Kuei Jin a Cainite/Kin Jin is a miserable wretched creature forever stuck in a Chih-mei state<br /> <br /> They are not <i>that</i> wrong, mind you. While the Kuei-Jin are technically a kind of Risen, the Cainites are the victims of a demonic blood curse<br /> The Book of Nod literally says: &quot;By calling up demons and listening to whispered wisdom he learned the way to make a child of his own.&quot; after detailing how Lilith helped him, implying Caine was not only a Ravenant but an infernalist, a proto-baali so to speak...<br /> <br /> So we have <b>Caine/Khayyin</b> [VtM] and his strange brood who are from the Kuei-jin point of view are barely more than a chih-mei (and the Nagaraja need to consume flesh echoes their &quot;origin&quot;)<br /> <br /> Now on Blood &amp; Silk p. 158 there is a &quot;gossip&quot;, not a 100% fact, just &quot;rumors&quot; about the Salubri, the spawns of Zao-Lat and about their potential to awaken their P'o and start their Dharmic journey<br /> <br /> Since it is a sidebar thing and a &quot;gossip&quot;, I called it quasi-canon<br /> The Salubri Valeren/Obeah is the carbon copy of the Kuei-jin Soul Discipline <b>Chi'iu Muh </b>and Zao-Lat demonstarated a very strong Howl of the Devil-Tiger behavior with the creation of the Baali<br /> <br /> BUT if we want to be more exact, I think the Way of Ten Thousand Screams is more likely Zao-Lat tried - it was the first Dharma before Xue's formulation of the Fivefold Way during the time of the Demon Warrior Empire, to advocate embracing the P'o in an attempt to achieve a perfect union with the Yama Kings. The reasoning behind this was that the Creator made them for a purpose - to keep the Great Cycle in motion. Those of the Ten Thousand Screams Dharma chose one of the Yama Kings to emulate and spent their unlives fulfilling their terrible purpose. This &quot;proto-dharma&quot; was hunted to extinction but its philosophy of harnessing the P'o were adapted by Xue in the Howl of the Devil-Tiger Dharma<br /> <br /> The main problem I think lies here: the barbarian learned at Xue's feet, but failed to understand, worse, he fled with the stolen knowledge, left behind his mess in the form of the Wu Zao (who are eager to mimic their father, aka. steal secrets of the Kuei-jin, also Mokur originalyl was a Jomon , the native of Japan so there is a nasty Emma-O connection too) and the top of that, he probably tried to walk a Dharma that was heretical even in the time of Xue OR a way that later became the Howl of the Devil Tiger but without the udnerstanding and grim determination behind it<br /> <br /> The Jade Tablets a bit reinforce this, Saulot not really udnerstood the Wheel of Ages or what is the Demon Emperor and twisted that little he managed to pick up<br /> Frankly, they killed for less, especially with the Ravnos being a thorn in their side thanks to Zapatashura not to mention the Danava","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T04:24:28-07:00","id":1561155,"title":"","content":"Even more than normal, almost nothing in this is certain.<br /> <br /> You're dealing with the connecting point of two of the messiest pieces of lore in the entire setting, not because they're complex, nuanced or ambiguous, but because they're straight badly written for special reasons.<br /> <br /> 1. Saulot is the most retconned character in the setting. 1st Edition Saulot is a good guy and that's it, and this is an important plot point that must remain possible. But many players and authors straight up abhor the notion, so we have recurring attempts to add uncertainty that haven't always been careful or thought through.<br /> <br /> 2. The Wan Kuei hate for the Kindred is a result waiting for a cause. Both lines were designed independently, then it was decided they're in a nonnegotiable war for Doylist reasons and all explanations for why are post-hoc and not well integrated into any lore.<br /> <br /> For both you have the same underlying problem:<br /> <br /> A. The original lore follows a clear direction, is well integrated with the setting and necessary for some of its themes. Saulot must offer hope of transcendence and redemption. The KotE must be philosophers open to any seeker of Enlightenment.<br /> <br /> B. A later decision demands a result without a real change in lore. It's post-hoc and tackled on without much thought. Saulot must be dubious and the KotE must be completely hostile to the Cainites.<br /> <br /> C. The &quot;solution&quot; is throwing half-baked ideas, and since none can really solve the conflicted stance, you keep throwing more.<br /> <br /> D. Authors take the opportunity to work in their own preferences, since it doesn't have to really be coherent with the rest.<br /> <br /> E. The result is an incoherent stack of lore bits with no real connecting tissue. You pick what you want and join however you want, because they're not complete enough to make sense.<br /> <br /> Specifically for the question in the title: nothing anyone knows. Saying &quot;Saulot did something and now the Kuei-Jin want all Cainites dead&quot; is the whole point, you fill by yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T08:31:51-07:00","id":1561162,"title":"","content":"It's never stated outright what happened with Saulot. <br /> <br /> The general speculation is that while studying under Xu, at some point Saulot's Beast gained sentience and took control over him. He fell into Shadow Soul, attempted to kill Xu and was banished. This also serves as the basis for &quot;good/bad Saulot&quot;. Sometimes Saulot is a good guy, sometimes he's a bad guy. The reason is that he can fall into Shadow Soul where his Beast takes control and causes him to do bad things. It also leads to this idea that he may have ended up splitting his beast and higher soul apart and that there is both a good Saulot and evil Saulot out there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T10:26:48-07:00","id":1561164,"title":"","content":"My personal take on it is similar; Saulot (with all the retcons/rewrites) seems to be perpetually unable to find a personal way of transcendence, and meanders through whether to reconcile with his Beast or tame it. The episode with Xue smacks to me of the classic trope where the pupil fails to succeed and jealously turns 180\u00b0 in frustration. If you accept Saulot as a progenitor of the Baali, his bloodlines seem like some sort of a field test of the two opposed philosophies.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wouldn't be surprised if he somehow was also responsible for the Children of Osiris.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":27477,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","user":"voidshaper","date":". 07-01-2026, 01:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T11:26:41-07:00","id":1561167,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>voidshaper</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561164#post1561164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My personal take on it is similar; Saulot (with all the retcons/rewrites) seems to be perpetually unable to find a personal way of transcendence, and meanders through whether to reconcile with his Beast or tame it. The episode with Xue smacks to me of the classic trope where the pupil fails to succeed and jealously turns 180\u00b0 in frustration. If you accept Saulot as a progenitor of the Baali, his bloodlines seem like some sort of a field test of the two opposed philosophies.<br /> <br /> Edit: I wouldn't be surprised if he somehow was also responsible for the Children of Osiris.</div> </div> </div> </div>My problem with this line of thought is that it doesn't explain the extent of the grudge, or why it affects the Wu Zao so thoroughly.<br /> <br /> At worst it would still make sense that some Wu Zao defected to the Kuei Jin side, but this is presented as simply off-limits with no good reason.<br /> <br /> As for the Children of Osiris, remember they're not an actual bloodline, just a religion. Their members are converters. We also have no strong reason to think they weren't in fact founded by Osiris or Isis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T12:15:35-07:00","id":1561168,"title":"","content":"It's an observation without knowing much Kuei Jin lore on my side, so just speculation. I'm curious though how the Salubri/Baali/Tremere/Children would fit into the Dharmas.<br /> <br /> The Children thing is wild speculation, I will admit. There is some wiggle room for Saulot as the 'Typhon' who sired Osiris and maybe the 'Thoth' who tutored Isis and Nephthys. Bringing back Osiris and then test-running the Spell of Life on him just feels like something Saulot would do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Custom Sorcery: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1487084-pattern-weaving-ananasi-sorcery-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">For Ananasi</a> | Mortal:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1509365-hekau-for-sorcerers\" target=\"_blank\"> Hekau</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1550552-ma%C5%A1ma%C5%A1%C5%A1%C5%ABtu-mesopotamian-sorcery\" target=\"_blank\">Ma\u0161ma\u0161\u0161\u016btu</a> | Necromancy:<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1514352\" target=\"_blank\"> Dust Path</a>, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1535508-dav20-older-lamia-lore?p=1536244#post1536244\" target=\"_blank\">P.o.Fertile Grave Soil</a> | Thauma: <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1513911-have-you-your-players-ever-used-disciplines-sorcery-for-scholarly-pursuits/page2#post1515316\" target=\"_blank\">Ars Notoria</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27477-voidshaper","name":"voidshaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27477_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T15:46:57-07:00","id":1561175,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561167#post1561167\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My problem with this line of thought is that it doesn't explain the extent of the grudge, or why it affects the Wu Zao so thoroughly.<br /> <br /> At worst it would still make sense that some Wu Zao defected to the Kuei Jin side, but this is presented as simply off-limits with no good reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>My personal headcanon is that Saulot was branded an Akuma. He didn't exactly sell his soul to one of the Yama Kings, but while studying with Xue he also studied from the Yama Kings. Saulot always seemed like he was fairly open to knowledge, both good and evil. Perhaps those studies were responsible for his awakening his Beast. Whatever the case, if it was discovered that he was secretly meeting and studying with the Yama Kings, the reaction to him would make sense. Even the reaction to the Wu Zao, as they would be viewed akuma adjacent. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-01T16:25:40-07:00","id":1561176,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561175#post1561175\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My personal headcanon is that Saulot was branded an Akuma. He didn't exactly sell his soul to one of the Yama Kings, but while studying with Xue he also studied from the Yama Kings. Saulot always seemed like he was fairly open to knowledge, both good and evil. Perhaps those studies were responsible for his awakening his Beast. Whatever the case, if it was discovered that he was secretly meeting and studying with the Yama Kings, the reaction to him would make sense. Even the reaction to the Wu Zao, as they would be viewed akuma adjacent.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Tbh my headcanon is that there's no major conflict between Cainites and Kuei-Jin. It's simply not a thing. In my games there are both types of undead all over the world, even if not evenly distributed, and any conflict or alliance is a local thing. The Wu Zao are not particularly hated.<br /> <br /> Even because I put a lot more emphasis on the person before the transformation, especially for Cainites, and most Wu Zao would be way closer culturally to local beliefs than to the foreign ideas brought by the person who just killed them.<br /> <br /> But I do imagine the relationship being weird in places. No amount of teaching will change that they're simply not similar creatures beyond the idea of undeath.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T14:47:28-07:00","id":1561203,"title":"","content":"DO they hate him, or is opposing him just the party line when the subject comes up? Because I can't recall some constant, massive effort being made by them to destroy him.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T16:05:02-07:00","id":1561206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561203#post1561203\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">DO they hate him, or is opposing him just the party line when the subject comes up? Because I can't recall some constant, massive effort being made by them to destroy him.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's the party line to justify a constant effort being made to persecute the Wu Zao.<br /> <br /> That said, fine observation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-02T23:56:37-07:00","id":1561218,"title":"","content":"For the Kuei-jin, the concept of a &quot;Clan&quot; in which you are Embraced is a very alien<br /> In their eyes the Kin-jin are all the same<br /> Some followers of the Song of the Shadow Dharma have taken up study of the various &quot;Dharmas&quot; that the western vampires seem to adhere - tho' they see those evebn less than the heretical Dharmas because no Cainite has ever progressed beyond the state of hin and their general ignorance of the spirit world, obvious marks of failure in the eyes of the Kuei-jin<br /> Because of their limited interractions, mostly based on field experiments, talking with ghosts and such sources they classified seven:<br /> The Hundred-Mask Clowns, referring to Clan Ravnos (tho' the Kuei-jin of Idia have a bit more experience with the servants of Zapatashura, had a run in with Kartarirya and his brood and possibly the Danava\u2026)<br /> The Shameful Path of the Ghost Bully, referring to Clan Giovanni<br /> The Silent Tiger Brotherhood, likely referring to Clan Assamite<br /> The Rut of the Pretentious Geisha, likely referring to Clan Toreador<br /> The Way of the Insufferable Flesh Gardners, likely referring to Clan Tzimisce<br /> The Inauspicious Order of Blood Devils, likely referring to Clan Tremere<br /> The Thousand Charming Company Men, likely referring to the Clan Ventrue<br /> <br /> So they have a limited understanding and view things through a different lens<br /> <br /> When they see a Wu-Zao, they not really see a &quot;Clan&quot; or &quot;Bloodline&quot;, a Wu is a &quot;Blood Family&quot;, a group bound together by their Court or for some common purpose and by a totem spirit called a nushi<br /> Wu-Zao means the &quot;Family of Zao&quot;<br /> <br /> From their point of view there is this unsually large wu, all share the mark of the Chi'iu Muh (tho' they not really proficient with it, but passed the stages when the Dragon's tear is a gemstone to become an eye, but not reached the stage to become a great blazing, pear-like orb in the center of the forehead) and unusally resilient and/or fast - Black wind and Iron Mountain Demon Arts - suggesting a deep connection to their P'o with a parmament Yin Imbalance judging by their looks and still low on their Dharma, stucking at blood drinking to get chi. And their common goal is pretty clear, since they usually in pairs, a thief capable of obtaining the secrets of the Thousand Hells and a scholar who could decipher those secrets<br /> They are Zao's Family, they are named after Zao-lat<br /> <br /> The Kuei-jin never refer to Zao-Lat without some sort of epithet attached to the end of the name; the most common is &quot;Zao-Lat the Traitor&quot;<br /> They heard the stories of the student of Xue, a thief, a despicable creature who benefited from Xue's compassion, learned at the feet of the master and stole his wisdom and fled<br /> But this is is where the knowledge usually stops, he is a footnote<br /> <br /> You see, if you are not a Mandarin in your Court or higher you are technically forbidden to have a talk and business with the Kin-jin, if you suspects someone is one or have proof, accidentally talked one, you have to report it to your superiors and let the honored ones deal with this<br /> Young Kuei-jin are kept in the dark so to speak for their own good<br /> With the Way of the Lone Walker ritual a Kuei-jin willingly and willfully could turns her back on the systems of court and wu by declaring herself heimin and to be a heimin have some benfits, while not having a Wo and be a loner, dance on the edge of sociatey means they are looked upon with contempt and distrust the Courts pioneered the practice of using heimin as messengers and intermediaries between themselves and the western Kindred, in exchange for ensuring the heimin safe passage through their territory.<br /> So there is a way for a Young Kuei-jin &quot;offically&quot; have contact but in turn the Heimin's words are treated with suspicion and what they might say? With a grain of salt.<br /> We are again back to rumors<br /> <br /> At first glance a Wu Zao is not that different from a Kuai-jin, they are lockals and behave mostly like them, except the lack of acces to the Yin and Yang World and talking with the residents of these realms (with possible Demon/Wraith/Spirit/Hengeyoaki/Hsien enemies they made along the way) - but this last part is not that obvious unless a said resident rats them out...<br /> Sure the lack of knowledge with etiquette and such, how a Kuei-jin should behave usually gives them away, but they could keep up the act if they are learned enough<br /> <br /> The Kuei-Jin have a few powerhouses of their own right, but that is a side effect of walking the road to the Houndred Clouds and Bodhisattvas are usually removes themself from society<br /> In the whole Middle Kingdom <b>only two</b> individuals exist who actually met Xue and were his contemporaries and still around: Thousand Crane Mother, the founder of the Dance of the Thrashing Dragon Dharma and The Most Serene Black Pearl Mistress, Mother of Shadows, the only living Arhat of the Bone Flowers physically remaining on Earth<br /> These two ladies are the only two people in the Middle Kingdom who been there and know what <i>really</i> happened <br /> <br /> The whole Zao-lat &quot;hatred&quot; is basically passed down rumors and cautionary tales<br /> It is a bit like the story of the guarded flower in the Russian legends<br /> In the classic narrative, an Emperor (or a Czar like Catherine the Great) is strolling through the palace gardens when they notice a single lonely guard standing at attention in a remote corner of the courtyard. The ruler asks what the sentry is guarding, but the soldier has no idea and simply says he was following orders<br /> Confused, the ruler summons the captain of the guard, who in turn checks the official written regulations. The records show that a guard was assigned to that exact post two centuries ago to protect a tiny flower that had sprouted in the stone. A daughter of a past Emperor had placed a sentry there so no one would step on it. However, because the order was never officially rescinded, soldiers had continued to stand watch every single day in the exact same spot, long after the flower had died and the courtyard had changed<br /> The story is often used to illustrate the phrase &quot;the way it's always done,&quot; symbolizing how organizations and institutions can blindly follow rules and traditions, wasting time and resources on things that are no longer relevant<br /> <br /> It is really like that, except those two ancient Kuei-jin no one around who been there, remember and can tell you the truth (and to be honest, even they not really know, back then Xue's students porbably were just mildy amusing to them)<br /> So it is really complicated to answer your question, we can puzzle together rumors, hints and even then we only would get a very rough picture what may happened","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T02:17:40-07:00","id":1561220,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561218#post1561218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Kuei-jin, the concept of a &quot;Clan&quot; in which you are Embraced is a very alien</div> </div> </div> </div>This is utter nonsense and a barrage of pure, abject orientalism.<br /> <br /> Of fucking course they know what a clan is. They're not imbeciles and the concept is as old in East Asia as anywhere else. Their own species not working like that is not a barrier to understand what a bloodline is.<br /> <br /> They understand the politics of a continent where they deal with some regularity with the Changing Breeds, all of them, Mages and Hsien and can't understand the concept of an undead creature that isn't one of them? Seriously!?<br /> <br /> Kin-Jin and Kuei-Jin are not the same type of creature, it's as simple as that, and after many thousands of years I'm sure a lot of them have figured this out. Measuring the Kin-Jin by their systems is as nonsensical as measuring the Garou.<br /> <br /> Above all, Kuei-Jin and Wu-Zao are both taken from the local population. You can have people who met when alive, family members, famous personalities, in both sides. They have the very human local cultural reference first, not their own species' one.<br /> <br /> Certainly they can have a policy of obscuring the matter for new arrivals, they can practice institutional prejudice and all that, this is not a unique Western European feature, but this notion that they're incapable of basic logic and just understanding concepts is ridiculous, and even more when they're explicitly philosophical in bent as their way to attain power and succor.<br /> <br /> If a white nerd in the internet can understand their culture (fictional as it may be), I'm sure an actual philosopher exploring the mystery of the Dharmas can understand what a contagious curse is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T03:11:26-07:00","id":1561224,"title":"","content":"I believe the traditional answer is \u201cHe got caught\u201d.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/28339-atticus-cleanclaw","name":"Atticus Cleanclaw","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2024"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"638"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T03:26:20-07:00","id":1561225,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561220#post1561220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is utter nonsense and a barrage of pure, abject orientalism.<br /> <br /> Of fucking course they know what a clan is. They're not imbeciles and the concept is as old in East Asia as anywhere else. Their own species not working like that is not a barrier to understand what a bloodline is.</div> </div> </div> </div>What you <i>think </i>and what was described in the supplements are two different things<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T10:41:44-07:00","id":1561243,"title":"","content":"Sounds like the supplement was using a fair amount of bad stereotypes when it was published.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T11:28:10-07:00","id":1561244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561220#post1561220\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is utter nonsense and a barrage of pure, abject orientalism.</div> </div> </div> </div>So the basic idea is that many Wan Kuei don't actually know much about Kindred. Kindred were always rare in Asia and for thousands of years the only Court that had extensive dealings with Kindred was the Thunder Court, and the other Courts consider them a hairsbreath away from all being heretical Akuma. The existence of Kindred was known, but the details were much less well known and most Wan Kuei didn't care.<br /> <br /> It was similar to how most Kindred would be hard pressed to tell you the difference between a Troll and an Ogre.<br /> <br /> Things changed during the Mongol invasion, as Kindred were more common among the Mongols. This is when the Wan Kuei really started researching Kindred, figured out how Clans worked and created rituals that could affect vampires of higher generation by targeting their ancestors with lower generation.<br /> <br /> Then, during the colonial era, when Kindred showed up again as invaders, they brought back a lot of their old research and knowledge.<br /> <br /> Currently, most older Wan Kuei have at least a surface level understanding of Kindred, and how clans and the Curse of Caine works. But for younger Wan Kuei, a lot of it is kept a mystery. This is very much by design.<br /> <br /> One of the recurring conflicts in Kindred of the East is the idea that older Wan Kuei intentionally try and keep younger Wan Kuei ignorant about a lot of things. They claim that by giving them too much unnecessary information, it will cause Running Monkeys to focus on things other than their spiritual enlightenment. Worse, knowledge they're not ready for can drive them into the arms of the Yama Kings.<br /> <br /> This paternalistic attitude is the root of a lot of the conflict in KotE, both between different Courts, Dharmas and Wan Kuei of different ages, especially in the modern world where younger Wan Kuei probably know a lot more than elders who still think electricity is a fad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-03-2026, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T12:09:47-07:00","id":1561246,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561225#post1561225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What you <i>think </i>and what was described in the supplements are two different things<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>And both are frequently subject to change! There was, in particular, a rather huge series of leaps in KotE, going from &quot;So mysterious&quot; in its core to &quot;So, there's been a running war between Indian Ravnos and the Celestial Tribe for ever since there were Ravnos. The Ravnos know that the Celestial Tribe are Hungry Dead and engage in Sabbat-like tactics to disrupt their operations, since they can embrace them en masse while the Celestial Tribe has to hunt down bodies that have reanimated themselves. To add to that, Quincunx loyalists also battle the Celestial Tribe for the newly reborn Flesh Eaters...&quot;<br /> <br /> So, the Ravnos definitely know, and anyone who manages to make any inroads with them can find out. There's also at least one family of Giovanni that likely knows (because ghosts are their business), and while they're not exactly keen on sharing secrets, it's still probably possible if you exchange favors. Everything is negotiable with licks; nothing is really off the tables, especially if it comes to something that might hurt their rivals.<br /> <br /> Not that it matters now. KotE is in a state of limbo, and the most popular interpretation of it is probably The Relentless Age, given that it cleaned out a lot of cruft and also got a boost by being featured in a Burgerkrieg video. So, while a fan work, it's probably got more cred in what's considered canon for KotE in the 20th anniversary stuff than anything that NuWW declares, since it declared KotE to not be a thing at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2},{"type":"\ud83d\ude00","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T12:18:14-07:00","id":1561249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561225#post1561225\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What you <i>think </i>and what was described in the supplements are two different things</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't said otherwise, I said the supplements say a lot of Bullshit. I said this earlier and said again with greater emphasis after your presentation.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I'm not well enough versed in KotE books to tell much, but I do know WoD books frequently present things with deliberate bias and some important contradictions, but here I'll take as granted that they were just orientalist enough to say this kinda seriously, they did had a lot of good will but a hard time actually putting the shoes of other cultures.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561244#post1561244\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So the basic idea is that many Wan Kuei don't actually know much about Kindred.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's by itself is reasonable to some extent, but doesn't explain a lot. The Camarilla isn't a lot different on the paternalistic knowledge gatekeeping, but Vampire recognizes that this doesn't means their success rate is astounding.<br /> <br /> But the main problems here are three:<br /> <br /> 1. The assumption that characters are incapable of grasping the concept of another undead type that doesn't correlate. Kin-Jin and Kuei-Jin are simply not the same thing and the differences are easy to grasp when you accept that. And all it takes is to hear them talk about their origins a little to notice the difference. It's not rocket science.<br /> <br /> 2. It greatly ignores actual geography and the logistics of commerce in favor of an imagined fencing between the Middle Kingdom and the rest of the world. Even if the Yama Kings are restricted to that area, people move. The KotE occupy an area that gets into contact with the Kindred sphere in several places, and would get even more contact by the sheer fact of people traveling plus commerce being a global phenomenon since always and just getting more so in the last centuries.<br /> <br /> 3. Our sore point is the Wu Zao. And wherever they are, we're talking about the local Kuei-Jin contacting them simply because they're there, so general ignorance don't apply. Why are the Wu Zao so thoroughly persecuted where they are? Why can't they ever interact, even without the Courts formally knowing? This is the part that demands most explanation and gets the least.<br /> <br /> Overall the whole idea is ludicrous as it only makes for obvious problems when students do meet Kindred, which they inevitably will given they're immortal beings.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T12:53:14-07:00","id":1561251,"title":"","content":"So<br /> 1) Wan Kuei don't really view themselves and Kindred as the same thing. Wan Kuei would consider themselves closer to Wraiths or Risen than to Kindred. The idea that they've actually died and gone to the underworld and then came back is central to their existence. Kindred never really die, at least not to the same extent. To Wan Kuei, Kindred are just an unusual type of supernatural being, hardly anything special beyond the fact that they share some superficial similarities to Yin cycled Wan Kuei. They would consider themselves as similar to Kindred as a Kindred considers itself similar to a werespider. There are some similarities, but they're not the same thing at all, and historically they were rare enough that they never mattered. Again, it's similar to how historically Vampires have never cared about Changelings. <br /> <br /> 2) The basic idea is that Kindred are outsiders to the supernatural world of Asia. Wan Kuei have extensive contact, including diplomatic contact and defense treaties with the Hegeyokai, Eastern mages, Hsien, etc. Kindred exist outside of that entire structure. This means that while there may be repercussions for a werewolf that kills a Wan Kuei, anyone can kill a Kindred at any time without any risk of political blowback. Conversely when Kindred try to kill Wan Kuei, this can end up pulling the Hengeyokai or other groups into the conflict and on the Wan Kuei's side. The fact that the various supernatural groups in Asia work together to a limited degree (due to shared opposition to the Yama Kings) has always been the main reason as to why Kindred struggled to penetrate Asia prior to colonialism.<br /> <br /> 3) Again, Wu Zhao exist outside of the supernatural structure in Asia. They have no friends and no allies. The Courts have ruled that interacting with a Wu Zao is illegal outside of certain intermediaries, so few younger vampires are willing to risk talking to one and being labeled akuma. The Wan Kuei Courts intentionally try and keep younger members ignorant because they think that will keep them more loyal. Basically they believe that allowing young vampires extensive interactions with individuals outside of, not just the court system, but the entire supernatural political structure, creates a slippery slope where those wan kuei may turn their backs on the courts and the 5 True Dharmas and eventually become akuma. That said there are younger wan kuei who interact with Wu Zao, or interact with demons, or do lots of other stuff that the Courts have deemed illegal. It does happen, but everyone tries to keep it secret and nobody will actually admit to doing it.<br /> <br /> Anyway, ultimately Kindred were always fairly rare in Asia until recently and, interacting with them was typically against the rules of the various Courts, so doing so risked being labeled an akuma and killed. As a result, historically most Wan Kuei had as little to do with Kindred as possible. It's only been fairly recent that Kindred have gotten more common and this is one of those conflicts within Wan Kuei society between the Courts and the Bamboo Princes, as the Courts try to pretend that the situation regarding Kindred hasn't changed in the last 100 years and refuse to update the rules, while younger vampires are out partying with Kindred every night at the local night club.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-03-2026, 03:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T14:33:19-07:00","id":1561252,"title":"","content":"Assuming that the documents that player characters may find and translate in The Transylvania Chronicle are authentic, the goal of either Saulot or the P'o of Saulot's divided self, drawing inspiration from the Wheel of Ages model of history, is:<br /> <br /> To advance the turning of the Wheel to the point where the August Personage abdicates the Throne of Heaven and a Demon Emperor ascends it;<br /> <br /> To be that Demon Emperor; and<br /> <br /> To then break the wheel and prevent its further turning, drowning the world in a demonic age that never ends.<br /> <br /> The first two parts of compatible with the teachings of Xue, in that *someone* will be the Demon Emperor, but the third part is a novel heresy. The Demon Emperor is supposed to have its victory and reign, according to those who believe in the Wheel, but the universe is then supposed to continue turning until the cycle starts over in a global or universal rebirth. Saulot is depicted in the Transylvania documents as out to rule as an anti-God forever and ever.<br /> <br /> The Wu Zao, for their part, are Saulot's eyes and ears in this, continuing their master's research into Hell's secrets for him while their clanmates to the west are discarded and hunted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11599,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","user":"Reasor","date":". 07-03-2026, 05:52 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T15:21:53-07:00","id":1561254,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561251#post1561251\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So</div> </div> </div> </div>My gripes with it:<br /> <br /> 1. Vampires don't care about Changelings because the Fae effectively don't interact, even in the same city. Where Kindred and KotE share space, they'll share a lot of it.<br /> <br /> 2. Kindred exist in Mongolia, old Persian Empire (all those countries ending in -stan), India and Russia. While country-level contact was a later thing, individuals travel between Europe, Africa and Asia as far as the Yellow River at least since antiquity. The idea of Asian isolation itself is considerably oversimplified and historically recent.<br /> <br /> In practice it's impossible for &quot;Asia&quot; (that's actually just a chunk of the continent, even if a big one) to be that impervious against foreign influence and visitors.<br /> <br /> This' anyway a far more nuanced presentation of the setting, thank you. And the reason they hate him so much remain nonexistent as far as anyone can tell, outside as maybe a useful tale to justify isolation.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561252#post1561252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wu Zao, for their part, are Saulot's eyes and ears in this, continuing their master's research into Hell's secrets for him while their clanmates to the west are discarded and hunted.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you assume the whole bloodline is utterly loyal in a way that makes little sense for them, since, again, they're locals and most never had contact with someone that ever had contact with as much as a child of Saulot, while their actual countrymen are just there.<br /> <br /> And that's assuming a very specific document is truer than most anything else in the setting. That's a valid headcanon, but a weak general theory for the setting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T15:59:04-07:00","id":1561256,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561254#post1561254\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Vampires don't care about Changelings because the Fae effectively don't interact, even in the same city. Where Kindred and KotE share space, they'll share a lot of it.<br /> <br /> 2. Kindred exist in Mongolia, old Persian Empire (all those countries ending in -stan), India and Russia. While country-level contact was a later thing, individuals travel between Europe, Africa and Asia as far as the Yellow River at least since antiquity. The idea of Asian isolation itself is considerably oversimplified and historically recent.<br /> <br /> In practice it's impossible for &quot;Asia&quot; (that's actually just a chunk of the continent, even if a big one) to be that impervious against foreign influence and visitors.<br /> <br /> This' anyway a far more nuanced presentation of the setting, thank you. And the reason they hate him so much remain nonexistent as far as anyone can tell, outside as maybe a useful tale to justify isolation.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think one of the big issues with KotE is that the gameline is primarily written with the focus on China, mainly eastern China. There's also a bit on Japan, but most of the other parts of Asia, like India or Korea, or Indonesia barely get more than a few paragraphs here or there. It's honestly not too different from base VtM where the main focus is on the US/Canada, with a bit of focus on Europe and then not nearly as much about anywhere else. <br /> <br /> This is a bit a problem with the current topic, because the Thunder Court in India has had long standing contact with Kindred, often they're in conflict, but occasionally Kindred and Wan Kuei will team up to fight against the Yama King's minions, or Wan Kuei on heretical paths (like the Face of the Gods). But we never really got any focus on India or how these interactions between Wan Kuei and Kindred actually looked like or played out. <br /> <br /> At least as far as the game setting goes, Kindred never really penetrated into eastern China or Japan the way they did in India. They were simply rarer there, again largely due to being spiritual outsiders and having no standing in the supernatural structure there. The Chinese Courts were also more conservative and strict then the Thunder Court, and were much more willing to label label someone for being an akuma for breaking minor laws (like speaking with a Kindred) than the Thunder Court. You always had Kindred in Asia, but they were never able to amass themselves into a power block, and were always stuck on the fringes of Wan Kuei politics. Ultimately Kindred never had enough power that they simply never mattered as far as the Courts' were concerned, so they primarily viewed Kindred with apathy. Except on the occasions Kindred did get enough power (such as the Mongol invasions or during colonialism) in which case the Courts' apathy turned to anger and xenophobia. <br /> <br /> You had something similar going on in Japan, where House Bishamon, which was intensely xenophobic, ruled for many centuries. They spent a lot of time trying to exterminate Kindred (and Wan Kuei from China) and would execute anyone accused of consorting with them. Meanwhile House Genji was more willing to work with Kindred and during the time they had control of Japan, Japan was pretty welcoming to Kindred. But then after WW2 they lost a lot of their power and Bishamon's taken control again. So the position of Kindred in Japan has been kind of yo-yoing back and forth for some time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-03T23:35:37-07:00","id":1561281,"title":"","content":"Personally I prefer that Kindred of the East are simply just the main 13 clans with names that makes sense due to the region.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T09:59:13-07:00","id":1561298,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561256#post1561256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think one of the big issues with KotE is that the gameline is primarily written with the focus on China, mainly eastern China.</div> </div> </div> </div>Basically that, plus the trope of isolation.<br /> <br /> In the 90s, particularly the early 90s, the idea of China as not only far, but closed, was very strong. The Cold War, the hard borders in Hong Kong and Taiwan and the Opium Wars still being mostly portrayed as China trying to stop foreign culture, all contributed to a vision in the US and its allies that the country was a cultural fortress.<br /> <br /> KotE drinks primarily from this source. It really is primarily Eastern China, basically Beijing and a few other provinces along the Yellow River, and it is China from the POV of then recent history of interaction with UK and US. It uses the regional influence of China as an excuse to generalize an already skewed view over a small area to a way larger one.<br /> <br /> Japan was a complicating factor, as it indeed had an isolation policy (historically specific), were now a US ally, had a strong conservative nationalist bent (due to how it was dealt with at the end of the War) mixed with a strong move to modernization, overall it was a country in internal conflict about its relationship with the US and that reflected on the US view over the rest of Southeast Asia.<br /> <br /> All that said, those are all things the games were in course to improve were it not for KotE getting such a backlash that it was mostly left aside despite having a strong fan base. And the result would probably be a lot more nuance and variation across courts, and less &quot;tongue in cheek&quot; references to the policies of China's Communist Party.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T10:15:12-07:00","id":1561299,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561281#post1561281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I prefer that Kindred of the East are simply just the main 13 clans with names that makes sense due to the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, and I understand the sentiment, but I have three reasons to disagree:<br /> <br /> 1. The game has fans. If it has fans, it has a right to be continued. It's a part of the WoD in the same way the Imbued are, no matter how much I prefer Hunters Hunted.<br /> <br /> 2. It's an interesting conceptual addition. Not the whole idea that Asia is a totally different world, but the idea of vampires that follow very distinct rules because the Kindred don't have a monopoly on immortality curses. The general gist of people climbing out of an artificial hell to retake their bodies and become this distinct variety of undead (with more emphasis on the dead part) is very cool.<br /> <br /> 3. While most Asian fans definitely want to play normal Cainites and have the Camarilla vs Sabbat conflict in their cities, the elimination of the KotE reeks of cultural erasure. Just as the introduction should have been done carefully, a removal isn't a simple matter, either, or it looks like the problem was the cultural diversity, to have tried.<br /> <br /> Overall correction is better than scrapping it. The games fared well in the many cases where it worked on improving, like the Banu Haqim. A similar approach to KotE would probably help.<br /> <br /> And the presence of Kindred, well, just add it. Seriously the setting won't change dramatically if it is revealed that several cities have Kindred and this was just little known in the US. It's not as if most US Kindred would notice if the Asian vampire they're dealing with is one of the other.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T10:43:17-07:00","id":1561300,"title":"","content":"A fair point Montparnasse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:04:20-07:00","id":1561302,"title":"","content":"Or, put another way, &quot;The 13 clans and their bloodlines encompass all the vampire types across mythology and pop culture... but never a jiangshi or penanggalan! Those are off limits!&quot; is quite... oddly selective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:30:37-07:00","id":1561306,"title":"","content":"By the way, the Penanggalan is possibly the only vampire with real widespread presence through myth. Out of the top of my head I can't remember any other that isn't heavily edited and spread by pop culture.<br /> <br /> The Jiangxi just wasn't edited and spread by US pop culture, it was by Chinese pop culture, based on a way milder original legend from Eastern China.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T11:36:00-07:00","id":1561307,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561249#post1561249\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't said otherwise, I said the supplements say a lot of Bullshit. I said this earlier and said again with greater emphasis after your presentation.<br /> <br /> Not to say that I'm not well enough versed in KotE books to tell much, but I do know WoD books frequently present things with deliberate bias and some important contradictions, but here I'll take as granted that they were just orientalist enough to say this kinda seriously, they did had a lot of good will but a hard time actually putting the shoes of other cultures.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That's by itself is reasonable to some extent, but doesn't explain a lot. The Camarilla isn't a lot different on the paternalistic knowledge gatekeeping, but Vampire recognizes that this doesn't means their success rate is astounding.<br /> <br /> But the main problems here are three:<br /> <br /> 1. The assumption that characters are incapable of grasping the concept of another undead type that doesn't correlate. Kin-Jin and Kuei-Jin are simply not the same thing and the differences are easy to grasp when you accept that. And all it takes is to hear them talk about their origins a little to notice the difference. It's not rocket science.<br /> <br /> 2. It greatly ignores actual geography and the logistics of commerce in favor of an imagined fencing between the Middle Kingdom and the rest of the world. Even if the Yama Kings are restricted to that area, people move. The KotE occupy an area that gets into contact with the Kindred sphere in several places, and would get even more contact by the sheer fact of people traveling plus commerce being a global phenomenon since always and just getting more so in the last centuries.<br /> <br /> 3. Our sore point is the Wu Zao. And wherever they are, we're talking about the local Kuei-Jin contacting them simply because they're there, so general ignorance don't apply. Why are the Wu Zao so thoroughly persecuted where they are? Why can't they ever interact, even without the Courts formally knowing? This is the part that demands most explanation and gets the least.<br /> <br /> Overall the whole idea is ludicrous as it only makes for obvious problems when students do meet Kindred, which they inevitably will given they're immortal beings.</div> </div> </div> </div>KotE needed the revision that many other groups got during the Revised. Just think of how much depth all the independent clans got in the Revised era compared to their pretty one note racist stereotypes. And since Kuei-jin appeared on the Eve of Destruction WW never had time for that revision, Onyx Path was never give a chance to do it and Paradox decided to ignore them totally instead of fixing. And here we are,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2357-sathriel","name":"sathriel","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"121"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T12:13:52-07:00","id":1561314,"title":"","content":"&quot;The Shameful Path of the Ghost Bully&quot;<br /> <br /> I laughed out loud at this! :-D","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\ude02","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3598-cajunkhan","name":"CajunKhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3598_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1700"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T13:31:05-07:00","id":1561315,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CajunKhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561314#post1561314\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;The Shameful Path of the Ghost Bully&quot;<br /> <br /> I laughed out loud at this! :-D</div> </div> </div> </div>Belive it or not, those names are totally official, not my headcanon - as written in <b>Dharma Book: Bone Flowers </b><img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-04T16:45:11-07:00","id":1561325,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561281#post1561281\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally I prefer that Kindred of the East are simply just the main 13 clans with names that makes sense due to the region.</div> </div> </div> </div>With Kindred of the Ebony Kingdom, it always had the somewhat negative reputation in the fandom of being about &quot;vampires in silly hats&quot; since they were just regular vampire clans with slightly changed names and perhaps slightly changed weakness. Some people liked this, some people didn't. Plus there's the inherently problematic idea of saying that various other culture's beliefs were actually European-style vampires who descend from the Biblical Cain the whole time.<br /> <br /> When you have the game spending a decade (or more) pushing this Biblical reading of the setting, it's can feel a bit problematic when that becomes the default assumption for other cultures. Like yes, in Ebony Kingdom they have their own, different myth for vampires, but it still comes off as Cane and Abel in silly hats. in contrast, while KotE had issues, I really liked the fact that the game was willing to approach the setting on its own terms rather than trying to fit everything in the Biblical, Cain and Abel context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-04-2026, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T11:49:01-07:00","id":1561352,"title":"","content":"I do like the notion that it's a party line that the Kindred of East dislike Saulot and the rest of his kind as uncultured rabble.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-05T16:22:39-07:00","id":1561356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561352#post1561352\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I do like the notion that it's a party line that the Kindred of East dislike Saulot and the rest of his kind as uncultured rabble.</div> </div> </div> </div>But that's about nationality, not species.<br /> <br /> Let's say a US citizen of British ancestry arrives in Beijing for tourism and ends up killed there. They end up in one of the Thousand Hells, claws their way out and manages through whatever means to start the path of a Dharma.<br /> <br /> They're a Kuei-Jin, but also mostly oblivious to Chinese culture. Not just they don't understand much of the courts, that would be expected, but the very fundamental cultural framework for the court. They are your regular obnoxious &quot;murica&quot; thinking they're now stuck away from civilization.<br /> <br /> On the other side, you have an Embraced Han Chinese, maybe caught when traveling abroad, maybe turned by a visiting Kindred. They're not a foreigner, they're someone who grew up in the same general cultural background and has no problem absorbing all the concepts and nuances of the Kuei-Jin Court.<br /> <br /> They're Kin-Jin, but completely integrated into the mindset and philosophy, if not yet in the specifics. They may have studied Confucius and Taoism, knows folk mythology, Buddhism and lots of other things, not just understand the basic concepts, but has them ingrained.<br /> <br /> Why should the Court so readily accept the one who's a Kuei-Jin, but won't ever understand their ways fully, and refuse the Kin-Jin who came from the same people surrounding them and already knows how to interpret the whole spiel in one go?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T05:53:29-07:00","id":1561380,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561356#post1561356\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why should the Court so readily accept the one who's a Kuei-Jin, but won't ever understand their ways fully, and refuse the Kin-Jin who came from the same people surrounding them and already knows how to interpret the whole spiel in one go?</div> </div> </div> </div>At that point we're getting into religious territory. The idea that the Wan Kuei were returned from hell at the behest of the Jade Emperor, for the higher purpose of saving the world from the Yama Kings is central to the Wan Kuei's existence. This means that the Wan Kuei have very specific duties under heaven's mandate, whereas the Kindred do not.<br /> <br /> Spiritually, the Wan Kuei have a divenly ordained obligation to assist other Wan Kuei in finding their path, even if those Wan Kuei are not from the local culture, whereas the Kindred are entirely outside of that divine mandate, regardless of what culture they grew up in. In fact, the Quincunx's aggressive attempts to spread the 5 &quot;true&quot; dharmas to all Wan Kuei, including places well outside of China, is a major source of conflict for the Wan Kuei and forms the basis of a lot of tension between the different Courts and the various heretical dharmas.<br /> <br /> It would be similar to asking why the Prince of New York would be willing to extend the Traditions to a Kindred from Africa, but not to a werespider from the Bronx. At the end of the day, the Camarilla's traditions and rules are intended for the Kindred, not for every creature that happens to feed on blood. Similarly the Wan Kuei's rules and obligations are directed towards other Wan Kuei, not everyone who was born in Asia or everyone who feeds on blood (note that they would also accept a foreign Wan Kuei in their ranks over a werespider that was born locally).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-06-2026, 11:32 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T11:56:56-07:00","id":1561395,"title":"","content":"So there's a religious idealogy that also plays apart of the strained relations with Kindred of East and the Kindred of Caine. That helps fill in more of the issues.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T21:47:45-07:00","id":1561408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561380#post1561380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At that point we're getting into religious territory.</div> </div> </div> </div>My point isn't to deny this, but to remind that culture matters to how they think about someone. The post I was responding to was specifically about regarding the Kindred as uncultured.<br /> <br /> Generalizations about culture make sense of based on culture, not species. The Wan Kuei have a duty to the new Wan Kuei, even if they're a foreigner, and no duty towards the Kindred.<br /> <br /> BUT their reasons to feel kinship towards the foreigner are another thing entirely. They may bond over the shared experience of escaping a Hell, but if we're talking someone appalled with lack of proper culture, helping this Wan Kuei is not a duty to be enjoyed.<br /> <br /> The local Kindred, likewise, may share no role in the Celestial Order, but is someone to feel kinship for to a certain degree. It's an equal in a sense the foreigner never will be.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying everyone would be overly attached to their countrypersons, or everyone is actually xenophobic, but trying to show how arguing about &quot;Kindred culture vs Kuei-Jin culture&quot; makes absolutely no sense. They share culture far more due to country than species.<br /> <br /> By the way: a Prince is perfectly capable of extending the Traditions to a werespider if they are aware of it. And Kindred being how they are it would be just a matter of the spider offering an advantage.<br /> <br /> Since Kindred society is primarily built on the need to manage resources (and have company) rather than religion, it's also plenty adaptive.<br /> <br /> And the Court may not have a duty to take care for the Kindred, but they can have alliances and a relationship nonetheless.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561395#post1561395\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So there's a religious idealogy that also plays apart of the strained relations with Kindred of East and the Kindred of Caine. That helps fill in more of the issues.</div> </div> </div> </div>Kinda, but not quite.<br /> <br /> Their religious obligation is to fight the Yama Kings, and to a lesser degree the Wyrm, but not in a blind interpretation (as many of them are Wyrm-tainted). Every splat in Asia fights the Wyrm in some form, except Mages sometimes. Has a lot to do with Exalted.<br /> <br /> While they will certainly be obliged to oppose a number of Kindred on grounds of this religious duty, they're not bound to declare war forever more on every Cainite. This is a cultural/setting thing mostly unrelated to their religion.<br /> <br /> More or less they just decided Kindred were too barbaric to be worth the effort. But somehow are worth a war in LA.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-06T22:48:15-07:00","id":1561413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561408#post1561408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But somehow are worth a war in LA.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is a very complex thing<br /> I will not bore you with the details, unlss asked, but the War in LA is a very complicated social, spiritual and military situation with several players on several levels and sides with potential long term consequences<br /> <br /> San Francisco by Night write about the Broken Mirrors a bit more detailed the the 1000 Hells (this also touches the Yomi influence)<br /> Along with them and Shadow War (this one even mentions one of the Jade Court' bodhisattvas voicing criticism against the campaign and concern - prophecy actually, that the Great Leap Outward would only weaken the Blood Court in the long run, although no one listened to him) and the Dharma Books they touch the subject<br /> <br /> <i>Some</i> Kuei-jin even have made the connection about the spreading Yomi-influence - or the reson behind it eg. the &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; - but generally they remained silent in fear of voicing their suspicions too loud<br /> <br /> For why it worth a War?<br /> It is complicated as I said, but the roots are in the Quincunx. It sought revenge against Western supernaturals for historical European imperialism in Asia. The invasion allowed them to aggressively expand their territories, spread their Dharma philosophies, and test their spiritual martial arts against Cainites, whom they viewed as parasitic barbarians<br /> The expansion provided opportunities to claim &quot;Dragon Nests&quot; (caerns and nodes) and this allowed the Wan Kuei to set up bubbles of consensus aligned with the Middle Kingdom, diminishing the influence of Western vampires<br /> <br /> It is not just conquest, not just a war for territory<br /> The borders of the Middle Kingdom are not set in stone, they actually move<br /> During the Victorian Age, there had been sightings of Wan Kuei in places like Istanbul and St. Petersburg.<br /> Expatriates have reached Chinatowns all over the world<br /> They not only spread influence on the material level but on the spiritual side like a spreading bloodstain on a white kimono<br /> The Dragon Nest and Dragon Line &quot;network&quot; they use (and sometime share with other supernaturals, esxcept the Little Gods, that realtionship is beyond sour) extends and with that the potential for them<br /> There always were K\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n, those wo have taken the Second Breath outside the Middle Kingdom and somehow managed to transcend their chih-mei phase but with the Great Leap Outward they became more aware of the K\u00e0nbuji\u00e0n's existance and their duty is to civlizie them\u200b<br /> ...and where the Kuei-jin go, in their shadow lingers Yomi as a lovely side effect and the Yama Kings are very &quot;supportive&quot; of this project (especially Mikaboshi, who \u200b\u200bnot only been a Japanese scholar and fang shih before his ascendence but a very good geomancer, he know how things work and he have his own incursion; his Hell, the Wicked City bled into the CyberRealm already) and quietly fan the flames because it is more opportunity for them to claim souls and spread Yomi's influence. Sure the Yama Kings have a cold and cordial relationship with the Western Hells and their Kings aka. Malfeas and the Maeljin but by all means they are not friends. But both sides knows it not worth the effort to go an all out war. The Great Leap Outward tipps the balance to their favor<br /> <br /> So this is layers upon layers upon layers, depending how deep you want to go<br /> There is not a neasy and short answer why the LA war worth the Kuei-jin's time and efforts<br /> <br /> But LA. the <b>New Promise Mandarinate</b>, providing a vital geopolitical and spiritual beachhead in the West. It the ultimate testing ground to prove that Eastern vampires could systematically dismantle, occupy, and govern a major Western Cainite domain but more importantly Los Angeles and its surrounding landscape contained powerful, untapped ambient Chi lines and spiritual sites.<br /> And on the other level The Ancestors feared Western corruption and Kinfolk-tainted forces bleeding into Asia. Weaponizing LA as a forward military base effectively pushed the frontline of the spiritual war away from the Middle Kingdom and onto the American mainland.<br /> and of course dominating the Pacific Rim's primary trade and cultural hub allowed Eastern factions to seize control of vital mortal shipping lines, smuggling routes, and criminal syndicates<br /> While the Mandarinate only achieved stability by making a desperate political deal with Anarch leader Jeremy McNeil they created the &quot;Quicksilver Court&quot; in Chinatown, essentially allowing some Anarchs to keep their territories in exchange for recognizing Kuei-jin oversight. This is actually a very interesting and kind of huge if you think about it. The Kuei-Jin view Cainites as spiritual dead-ends after all, granting them quasi-Chih-mei status while they behave even if it was not realyl their plan to begi nwith and required a little arm twisting (and the downfall of the strict traditionalist Mandarin Hao Wei Liang, who was forced to commit ritual suicide by facing the sun in October 1999, leaving Fu Han-wu , the Minister of Pearly Righteousness\u200b and the compromise-driven Ancestor Jiejie Li to manage the uneasy truce\u200b\u200b\u200b) <br /> <br /> I'm not sure properly we could dissect this topic here and would it be a topic derlaing or not, since it is not really relevant why the Kuei-jin &quot;hates&quot; Saulot and his blood family","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T00:37:37-07:00","id":1561414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561413#post1561413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The &quot;Great Leap Outward&quot; is a very complex thing</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd rather say &quot;inconsistent&quot;, but I think you can go in details. It is absolutely related to the reason why they hate Saulot, as in the end they do as an excuse (not the only one) to justify the conflict.<br /> <br /> The conflict is the point, and I don't think a well thought one. It removes Kindred from China by making the place too hostile, and give LA a &quot;nice&quot; crossover war that I think was mostly useless and could have been achieved in better ways.<br /> <br /> For now your current answer just proves my thesis: the conflict is justified by some things that didn't required an actual large scale war, some half-baked ideas to try and say they did, and a lot of &quot;generic xenophobia/Chinese Fear&quot; to spice things up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T01:28:45-07:00","id":1561415,"title":"","content":"I think, and don't take this as lecturing or anything like that, and with all due respect it seems you forgot, the World of Darkness is a <i>setting</i><br /> <br /> Not &quot;Earth just with Vampires&quot;<br /> <br /> It is a subtile difference, like how Earth-616, the Marvel comic universe is different slightly of the MCU or any movie/live action adaptation is same same but different<br /> WoD is not Earth, it is its own setting, fictional universe with it own rules and views<br /> You want to apply stricly IRL Earth vallues to something that never had those to begin with - had something very similar, but never really been chained by it<br /> You don't question the setting of D&amp;D / Spelljammer for not making &quot;sense&quot; because it is wastly different, but WoD built on Earth, easy to say &quot;oh it is just Earth with some added furries with claws and vampires&quot;<br /> <br /> But it is not - the core vallues are very very similar but not the same<br /> <br /> Shadowrun is a good example how things could change the setting<br /> <br /> WoD is based on Earth but what are &quot;bad stereotypes&quot; or make no sense are part of that <i>setting</i><br /> You don't like it? What is the golden rule? Change it.<br /> As the Analyst said: &quot;<i>You think you hold all the cards, because you can do whatever you want in this world. I say, go for it. Remake it. Knock yourselves out. Paint the sky with rainbows. But here's the thing. The sheeple aren't going anywhere. They like my world... They crave the comfort of certainty</i>.&quot;<br /> <br /> What is in the KotE in the <b>setting</b> make <i>sense</i><br /> What you call half-baked ideas and generic xenophobia/Chinese Fear in a sense hardwired into the whole thing, it is built on it<br /> <br /> Try to see it from outside and not through the lenses of your expectations and dare I say prejudices","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T10:55:05-07:00","id":1561421,"title":"","content":"They do mention that the world of darkness is like our world, but darker, grimmer and more corrupted then the real world.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T14:03:24-07:00","id":1561433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561408#post1561408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My point isn't to deny this, but to remind that culture matters to how they think about someone. The post I was responding to was specifically about regarding the Kindred as uncultured.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is, for the Wan Kuei, their culture isn't mortal culture. It's not about being Chinese or Japanese or Indian. It's not about being able to quote Confucius or the Mahabharata. Their culture is about being the Wan Kuei, the direct descendents of the Ten Thousand Immortals. People who have gone to hell and then crawled back out at the behest of the Jade Emperor. The Wan Kuei's culture is much bigger than geographical mortal cultures. That's also the big reason why they look down on most other supernatural beings. Other supernatural beings, whether shapeshifters or Kindred or mages, just happened to be born into their power or fell into it. The Wan Kuei earned it when they pulled themselves out of hell through their own personal efforts and that forms the basis of their culture.<br /> <br /> That said, there are certain geographical elements - the Wan Xian were commanded to watch over Asia, only people who go to the Ten Thousand Hells can become Wan Kuei, etc. But the culture of the Wan Kuei is not the culture of mortals. Whether one of the Hungry Dead was born in China or India or Japan or Southeast Asia or even in America is much less important than the fundamental fact of being one of the Wan Kuei. Where your spent your mortal years growing up is not very important except to a subset of bigoted individuals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-07-2026, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T18:53:38-07:00","id":1561443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561415#post1561415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, and don't take this as lecturing or anything like that, and with all due respect it seems you forgot, the World of Darkness is a <i>setting</i><br /> <br /> [.....]<br /> <br /> Try to see it from outside and not through the lenses of your expectations and dare I say prejudices</div> </div> </div> </div>See <a href=\"https://&#91;URL=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=AxV8gAGmbtk&quot;\" target=\"_blank\">Minisode - The Thermian Argument - YouTube</a><br /> <br /> But to address a couple of specific points:<br /> <br /> There has actually been a decent amount of discussion around D&amp;D in recent years criticizing how it has traditionally approached the issue of race, because it is reflective of historical attitudes and practices that are pretty Yikes.<br /> <br /> Similarly, I'm not even a huge comic books nerd, and I know that conversations around issues of representation and values and how they reflect or connect with the real world are pretty much endemic; there's literally a kerfuffle right now because someone who worked for Marvel is claiming that the Civil Rights analogy around stuff like the X-Men was never part of the original authorial intent.<br /> <br /> The World of Darkness is our world with a horror-fantasy coat of paint. Trying to act like it should somehow be treated as this completely fantastical space that can't be analyzed in terms of how the real world opinions and biases of the authors are reflected in their creation seems quite unreasonable to me, or that those influences aren't going to affect how different people engage with the setting based on their own real world experiences.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T20:53:39-07:00","id":1561445,"title":"","content":"Off topic, but the X-men analogy was always kind of awkward to me. Like, some mutants are walking nuclear bombs. It's understandable why someone would would be weary of a person whose power puts them and the entire neighborhood at risk living next door. And it's understandable why the government might want to make a list to track such individuals and their powers, especially when you have a subset of those people regularly carrying out criminal activity, mass murder, assassination, terrorism, acts of war. etc. Whether I agree or not, I can see the reasoning behind it.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile in real life, there's no reasonable reason to not want a member of a minority or a member of the LGBTQ+ community living next door. Likewise, there's no reasonable argument for the government tracking such people.<br /> <br /> While there was an effort to make the X-men and mutants stand-ins for Civil Rights, I don't think that analogy really holds up once you start examining it. There's no reason to be worried about some random person that's gay. There is a reason to be worried about some random person who can blow up your city by thinking about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-07T22:11:40-07:00","id":1561446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561415#post1561415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shadowrun is a good example how things could change the setting</div> </div> </div> </div>(Makes creaky, unsteady motions with hand) Eh, ehhhh. Shadowrun had to put in serious effort to backpedal some of its more ridiculous early claims (&quot;Ethnic prejudice is a thing of the past because every hatemonger is concentrated on metas now!&quot;), which is only deigned to do by SR5. In some cases it also tried to paint anti-metahuman sentiment as reasonable, particularly in the case of trolls, and while trolls are huge, so are some people, and trolls are only marginally more likely to survive being shot by a bog standard heavy pistol, barring weird early armor and ammo rules (looking at you, SR1). And in that case, well, it's clearly the armor and its automatic damage resistance successes that's doing the heavy lifting.<br /> <br /> Moreover, FASAnomics figures large in how runners live, pay bills, and otherwise exist. Look too closely at it, and it might just fall apart.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T01:20:42-07:00","id":1561448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shadeprowler</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561415#post1561415\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think, and don't take this as lecturing or anything like that, and with all due respect it seems you forgot, the World of Darkness is a <i>setting</i></div> </div> </div> </div>And with all due respect, that's the point.<br /> <br /> It's not reality, and it's not religion. It's meant to be examined, evaluated, criticized. It confronts and reproduce real values through fiction. It is a message, a creation, a work with flaws and perspectives backed in it. It has intent, it tries things, it succeeds and fail. It's neither infallible or sacred, and it's not meant to be.<br /> <br /> Not even fixed, it changes as new authors work on it, up to and including dozens of authors that publish in the Vault, dozens or hundreds more that post their creations here and in other places through the internet, thousands upon thousands of Storytellers running the game and deciding how to apply it.<br /> <br /> Being a TTRPG setting that went through so many hands it is messy and full of holes. It has an authorial goal to be open to interpretation, to have loose ends, unanswered questions and untrustworthy answers.<br /> <br /> WoD in particular is a critique. It was from start made to challenge stereotypes and prejudice. It just isn't perfect, and carries the weight of the culture of its creators. And White Wolf knew that, so much so that such criticism was there since always and they received, accepted, used it to improve.<br /> <br /> So yeah, don't know if you noticed, but I didn't said any of that wasn't the setting, I said it was bad storytelling. And you keep avoiding this to show more and more of the setting, without ever engaging what I actually said.<br /> <br /> You're the one constantly looking at it from the inside. Treating book content as if it was some unavoidable archaeological evidence rather than made up stuff. Not a now thing, by the way, you never engage people's questions from any other perspective, its always mapping your theories of correct interpretation of theology with the assumption that all the texts you like are some hard truth.<br /> <br /> Even trying to throw some bullshit saying that people like the WoD as validation? You fucking read what actual players like me say? No one in their right mind thinks WoD is perfect, even if we don't agree on what parts are a problem. All over those forums and many others there are fans bashing similar takes, many way harsher than me.<br /> <br /> Then &quot;prejudice&quot;, eh? That confirms what I've been suspecting for some time. I know exactly the kind of people that would use this word in this context for this defense in such a post. So I think I have to thank you for the kindness of making things clear.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T01:47:25-07:00","id":1561451,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561433#post1561433\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is, for the Wan Kuei, their culture isn't mortal culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think this is completely true, but more importantly I don't think this makes for a good take on the setting.<br /> <br /> Culture is a layered thing. I am Brazilian, I'm also a woman, a nerd, a WoD fan, psychologist, bank clerk, and many other things. All of those are my culture, there's no negation.<br /> <br /> More importantly, which is stronger to my identity is a personal characteristic, mutable even.<br /> <br /> A character that identifies only with the culture of their splat just sound flat to me, no matter how detailed this culture may be. A society that is defined solely for one factor is equally flat. It is both unrealistic and boring. Always preferred takes on the WoD where the fact it is the Earth-but-Darker meant supernatural shenanigans got layered with mundane questions.<br /> <br /> So, for me, a Kuei-Jin from China is a Kuei-Jin, but is also from China. They can pretend this makes no difference. They can believe it. But it's just not true. Hence my criticism.<br /> <br /> Now, specifically about someone who would look upon others as &quot;uncultured rabble&quot;? That's the attitude of someone with a particular kind of pride, and this pride won't come from a set of values they're regularly taking new recruits to teach from scratch. It isn't pride over what they conquered, either. This is pride over the kind of education the other part can't get. The Kindred can learn the Dharmas just fine, even if not benefit from them, so this is not the culture they're talking about.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T09:08:39-07:00","id":1561471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561451#post1561451\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now, specifically about someone who would look upon others as &quot;uncultured rabble&quot;? That's the attitude of someone with a particular kind of pride, and this pride won't come from a set of values they're regularly taking new recruits to teach from scratch. It isn't pride over what they conquered, either. This is pride over the kind of education the other part can't get. The Kindred can learn the Dharmas just fine, even if not benefit from them, so this is not the culture they're talking about.</div> </div> </div> </div>The thing is though, Wan Kuei at the core are intended to be a cross cultural splat. India, China and Japan are all very different cultures, but when it comes to Wan Kuei society, it doesn't matter. They're all viewed as equals and all treated the same. There are certain bigots who will look down on one group or another because of their mortal culture, but as a whole Wan Kuei society and their Courts are above and beyond mortal culture. <br /> <br /> It's no different than the Camarilla. When a Kindred enters a domain and asks the Prince to stay in his city, it doesn't matter what race, or gender or ethnicity the vampire is. It doesn't matter where they grew up or what religious beliefs they have. It doesn't matter if they can't quote the Bible or Shakespeare. It doesn't matter if that Kindred was born and Embraced in Africa. What matters is that they're a Kindred and that they're familiar with the Camarilla's Traditions. The Camarilla's culture is much more important than any particular mortal culture.<br /> <br /> And this goes for pretty much every World of Darkness splat altogether. For werewolves, one's Tribe is generally much more important than one's human culture. The same thing is true for Mage and their Traditions. A Celestial Chorister isn't going to care if a member of their Tradition was born in Asia or South America. <br /> <br /> Of course you do have individual exceptions. Everyone has prejudices. Some Kindred will look down on other vampires because of their mortal stock - because that vampire is black, or Irish or came from Asia. But as a whole, the Camarilla doesn't operate that way, and it's the same for the Wan Kuei. Mortal culture becomes a lot less important after someone has taken the Second Breath. And no matter how much a Kindred or Werewolf or Mage studies the words of the Dharmas or listens to stories about escaping from Hell or being chosen by the Jade Emperor, none of that is equal to actually living those things, which is where the Wan Kuei's sense of pride comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T09:27:48-07:00","id":1561472,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561471#post1561471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The thing is though, Wan Kuei at the core are intended to be a cross cultural splat. India, China and Japan are all very different cultures, but when it comes to Wan Kuei society, it doesn't matter. They're all viewed as equals and all treated the same. There are certain bigots who will look down on one group or another because of their mortal culture, but as a whole Wan Kuei society and their Courts are above and beyond mortal culture.<br /> <br /> It's no different than the Camarilla. When a Kindred enters a domain and asks the Prince to stay in his city, it doesn't matter what race, or gender or ethnicity the vampire is. It doesn't matter where they grew up or what religious beliefs they have. It doesn't matter if they can't quote the Bible or Shakespeare. It doesn't matter if that Kindred was born and Embraced in Africa. What matters is that they're a Kindred and that they're familiar with the Camarilla's Traditions. The Camarilla's culture is much more important than any particular mortal culture.<br /> <br /> And this goes for pretty much every World of Darkness splat altogether. For werewolves, one's Tribe is generally much more important than one's human culture. The same thing is true for Mage and their Traditions. A Celestial Chorister isn't going to care if a member of their Tradition was born in Asia or South America.<br /> <br /> Of course you do have individual exceptions. Everyone has prejudices. Some Kindred will look down on other vampires because of their mortal stock - because that vampire is black, or Irish or came from Asia. But as a whole, the Camarilla doesn't operate that way, and it's the same for the Wan Kuei. Mortal culture becomes a lot less important after someone has taken the Second Breath. And no matter how much a Kindred or Werewolf or Mage studies the words of the Dharmas or listens to stories about escaping from Hell or being chosen by the Jade Emperor, none of that is equal to actually living those things, which is where the Wan Kuei's sense of pride comes from.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've generally spent less time on specific locations and characters within the setting than I have on general aspects (e.g. the Umbrae), but this doesn't quite jive with my personal experience of the World of Darkness as a setting. Groups like the Camarilla aren't concerned with issues of race and mortal culture in the same way modern North American society is &quot;colour-blind&quot; or &quot;doesn't see race.&quot; It's absolutely still present and important in the experiences of characters in the setting, it's just less often to be explicit or formalized/legalized.<br /> <br /> Concerns around mortal racism, sexism, queerphobia, etc., frequently feature in the backstories of NPCs, though I must admit that I don't have a specific example clearly in mind; extremely confident I could find one if you insist on me demonstrating that particular point.<br /> <br /> So much of how the fleshing-out of the Banu Haqim was justified without being regarded as a retcon is basically just to wave at Orientalism: most European Kindred were happy accepting a racist caricature to the extent that it became the stereotype.<br /> <br /> The Wendigo/Galestalkers (at least pre-W5) were intensely tied up in the culture and politics of their Kinfolk, to give just one obvious example.<br /> <br /> The Technocracy is widely recognized as being intertwined with the capitalist imperialism of the European colonial powers.<br /> <br /> Referring to the Wan Kuei specifically, the Quincunx is not one big happy family of Kuei-jin who ignore the boundaries of mortal culture, with some significant differences in culture and mythology between Courts that are often reflective of the mortal cultures they emerged from. <br /> <br /> There's a laundry list of examples of how mortal culture, and prejudices, are interwoven into the supernatural underworlds of the World of Darkness, because most of the characters in it grew up in those mortal cultures to some extent or another, and were influenced by them. The idea that all of that just flickers out of existence after an Embrace or the First Change seems unlikely.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25886-kharnov","name":"Kharnov","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"683"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T15:14:38-07:00","id":1561489,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kharnov</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561472#post1561472\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've generally spent less time on specific locations and characters within the setting than I have on general aspects (e.g. the Umbrae), but this doesn't quite jive with my personal experience of the World of Darkness as a setting. Groups like the Camarilla aren't concerned with issues of race and mortal culture in the same way modern North American society is &quot;colour-blind&quot; or &quot;doesn't see race.&quot; It's absolutely still present and important in the experiences of characters in the setting, it's just less often to be explicit or formalized/legalized.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the same time though, these are not institutionalized policies. A prince might be misogynistic and look down on women, but he's going to run into problems pretty quickly if he starts talking down to a thousand year old Methuselah just because she's a woman. The same is true for vampires who bring other mortal prejudices with them. The Traditions are pretty clearly the most important part of Kindred society and any vampire who starts breaking those because of mortal prejudices is going to get a reality check fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> That's not to say that there aren't any vampires who engage in obvious actions based on mortal prejudices when dealing with other vampires, but rather that those tend to be the exceptions. You certainly have vampires who look down on women or black people, but at the same time Camarilla culture would not condone those racist or sexist vampires actions.<br /> <br /> This is also true for with Wan Kuei. There may be some members of the Quincunx who look down on non-Chinese Wan Kuei, but at the same time Wan Kuei culture recognizes that Arhats come from all regions and all groups, so even the most racist members would have to at least give lip service to the equality of Wan Kuei from India or Southeast Asia. In fact, with Wan Kuei, even a fairly racist Thousand Crane from China will likely be more respectful towards a Thousand Crane from India than to a young Devil Tiger from China.<br /> <br /> Again, in both cases you absolutely have individuals who are racist or sexist, but those don't really reflect the rules of the society that they're a part of. Both with Wan Kuei or the Camarilla the central idea is one of equality between members of their splat type. Further, when you do have issues, those tend to be more reflected by supernatural standing - members of clans in the Camarilla look down on one another, or members of different Paths will treat each other differently. As a general rule, within supernatural communities, the supernatural differences between individuals tend to be more important than mortal differences. That's where you start to run into semi-insitutionalized rules, like the treatment of Malkavians or Ravnos.<br /> <br /> So it's not so much a matter of being color blind, but rather that the colors that get the most focus are not skin color but supernatural color, especially as vampires get older and more and more divorced from their mortal lifetimes","signature":"","edited":{"userid":741,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","user":"AnubisXy","date":". 07-08-2026, 06:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1},{"type":"\ud83d\udc4e","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T15:42:46-07:00","id":1561491,"title":"","content":"That's true that most elders and methsulahs usually find such things as skin color, sexual orientation, gender and even religious idealogy become very trivial and just smirk at the younger ones for such limited thinking.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;Power that needs to advertise itself is already losing&quot; Grand Admiral Thrawn <br /> <br /> &quot;Coronation Starscream? This is bad comedy!&quot; Galvatron","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27361-lysander","name":"Lysander","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar27361_11.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2022"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T17:26:58-07:00","id":1561493,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561491#post1561491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true that most elders and methsulahs usually find such things as skin color, sexual orientation, gender and even religious idealogy become very trivial and just smirk at the younger ones for such limited thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well it does help that the Embrace seems to automatically turn all vampires bisexual. /s<br /> <br /> I imagine that holding onto religion was more understood by the Elders when the Road of Heaven was still a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26432-jagnestormskull","name":"JagneStormskull","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26432_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-08T17:54:43-07:00","id":1561494,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561471#post1561471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The thing is though, Wan Kuei at the core are intended to be a cross cultural splat. India, China and Japan are all very different cultures, but when it comes to Wan Kuei society, it doesn't matter. They're all viewed as equals and all treated the same.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're reading too much on the in-game official stance of those groups and attributing to the setting a posture it, at the very least, isn't actually promoting, though it may be a valid interpretation.<br /> <br /> Anyone with actual experience in institutional prejudice can tell you that's exactly what those institutions say. Bigots don't say they're bigots because they don't think they're bigots. They hide precisely behind the narrative that &quot;it does not matter&quot;.<br /> <br /> Bigotry is also very subtle. They speak their minds openly only when very secure, but they practice their discrimination through a miriad small ways that strangle you when put together.<br /> <br /> Not to say that the setting several times said quite the opposite.<br /> - European Kindred look down on New World Kindred.<br /> - The Banu Haqim treated as a stereotype for centuries, which was embraced by the setting rather than retconned.<br /> - No one knows what to say about Kindred from Africa. Or Asia. Or South America, even if they're from actual, known Kindred Clans.<br /> <br /> So... I wouldn't say this reading is THE official, no. Not even for KotE itself despite all the bad orientalism. It's an option. By all means, if your group doesn't like to explore this, you shouldn't, and I think the space for this interpretation is good.<br /> <br /> But for the people that study or live prejudice of this kind daily, a lot of those statements of institutional magnanimity read exactly as what they would say if it was a lie. Because the core of it is: &quot;we don't see color/culture/gender, so we don't talk those things&quot;, and avoiding this open talk is the actual point.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lysander</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561491#post1561491\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's true that most elders and methsulahs usually find such things as skin color, sexual orientation, gender and even religious idealogy become very trivial and just smirk at the younger ones for such limited thinking.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, sure.<br /> <br /> It's interesting that people like to hyperfocus on how Elders are frozen in time and don't follow modern conventions, usually to justify having the character avoid certain themes, but they are super forward with minorities, yes.<br /> <br /> No, thanks. I think that's bullshit, and against the spirit of the setting. Also, as said above, not at all what the books actually say the setting <i>is</i>, rather what some people within it <i>say</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T07:47:15-07:00","id":1561517,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>monteparnas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561494#post1561494\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think you're reading too much on the in-game official stance of those groups and attributing to the setting a posture it, at the very least, isn't actually promoting, though it may be a valid interpretation.</div> </div> </div> </div>A big part of KotE is the idea that the Quincunx wants to get everyone on the 5 main Dharma paths. It doesn't matter where those people are from. Like even the most racist member of the Quincunx would rather see Indian Hungry Dead on the 5 Dharma paths than messing around on heretical paths. One could argue that's simply pragmatism as the Quincunx believes that heretical paths are more likely to eventually end with the Wan Kuei in service to the Yama Kings. One could also argue that there's a certain amount of racism in the Quincunx pushing calling all of the other paths heretical and pushing them (though this is somewhat backed up mechanically by the fact that none of the heretical paths have produced an Arhat).<br /> <br /> Ultimately there is a sense of fraternity among the Hungry Dead, even if it's simply one based on pragmatism and a shared escape from Hell and opposition to the Yama Kings. Even for extremely racist Wan Kuei, most of them believe that it's better if other Wan Kuei, even from groups they don't like, oppose the Yama Kings than for them to end up joining the Yama Kings. Racism, sexism, etc exists, but it's going to primarily be directed towards mortals than towards other Hungry Dead, if only because directing racism, or sexism towards a respected Mandarin is likely to result in a Moment of Blindness.<br /> <br /> No one is going to become a respected elder if they demonstrate disrespect towards those who have walked the path before them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T16:22:24-07:00","id":1561535,"title":"","content":"I think one of the biggest problems discussing the Cainite v KoE emnity is that you are looking at it from the modern lense here, especially in regards to nationality and culture. This emnity isn't something -new- there's references to it in the in-lore ancient texts and stories. The Ercyes Fragments hint at it with its prophecies which could be as far as Second City era, since they would be written before Brujah/Ilyes' diablerie by Troile. The history of the Clans presented in their clan books show some of the wars; mainly Tzimisce / Kartarirya, Ravnos / Chandraputra, Nosferatu / Unknown Methulselah, settling in Harappa area and fighting wars with KoE in Mahenjo-Daro. Clan Book Lasombra Revised mentions broods before 1300 BC and 1100 BC in the Asianic areas. Overall the emnity between groups goes back at least 4-5000 years. <br /> <br /> On to gender/race. Id like to refer to Clanbook Lasombra Revised Pg 16's aside &quot;What Manner of Creature&quot; as an example of the Game/Devs/Setting explicitly stating that in general older Kindred don't care about such things. Are there Sexist or Racist Kindred? Sure are! Critias for example is a Pedophile and only feeds off young men, but these kinds of character's are outliers for the setting as a whole. This is also the reason that when read through the core books, the mention of gender/race doesn't appear till the Clan/Bloodline sections where they are talking about background. It really isn't all that important to the game as a whole, unless the players want to make it important. Don't forget this -is- a game. If players want to delve into race politics in their city, and as a table agree on it, then they're free to do so, but the game itself doesn't require it, push it, and functions just the same if every character is an androgynous statue. <br /> <br /> Back on topic to Saulot. There really isn't much information on Xue to be honest. Hell we know more about Caine, and the first three Generations than we know about Xue. I think personally, that the involvement is more of a rivalry between students rather than a master/student issue. To say, Xue had multiple students at the time, Saulot being one, and one or more of the other student's took umbrage on the &quot;outsider&quot; being able to learn at the master's feet thus the story of the &quot;stolen&quot; teachings. You can see this kind of parallel with Saulot and his childe Mokur's own students in the Lair of the Hidden book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3},{"type":"\u2615","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26219-aydoo","name":"Aydoo","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2026-07-09T20:39:05-07:00","id":1561549,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aydoo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1561153-what-on-earth-does-saulot-do-in-the-east-making-all-wan-kuei-hate-him?p=1561535#post1561535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think one of the biggest problems discussing the Cainite v KoE emnity is that you are looking at it from the modern lense here,</div> </div> </div> </div>The setting is clear that most vampires on both sides know next to nothing about the other.<br /> <br /> Vampires older than 500 years are exceedingly rare even in Europe, they're not making policy, they're plotting from the shadows of shadows if concerned at all.<br /> <br /> Add to that how specific and apart conflicts are among them: neither long contacts, nor big areas, or close their populational centers. The one big exception is India/border, but it IS national since it is only that area and outside it no one cares, few even know.<br /> <br /> Clanbook Lasombra is a fluke, the game is full of them since there are many authors and they are not a monolith.<br /> <br /> So I'm not convinced the conflict is explained well enough, I still don't see a point for it as a narrative element, and I stand that mostly the setting does not follow an assumption that old vampires are diversity-friendly.<br /> <br /> I do agree with the conclusion, I said it myself. If anything, exploring such themes is within the spirit of the game, but it's not its goal. It must be an open possibility, something the setting neither endorses or deny.<br /> <br /> We can't know even if the whole problem with Saulot happened at all, or be completely sure he was there (though that is likely). What I don't like is how this is a weak connection to how the Wu Zao are treated today.<br /> <br /> But I do like your point: we don't actually know if the grudge is the way it is told. In fact, I think we can't even say how old it really is. If most of the time the actual Vampires discussing this are no more than 4 or 5 centuries old, and even those are hard to believe, the whole enmity could be from just a few centuries ago and no one would notice.<br /> <br /> My bigger point, though: why write it like that? What does it adds, it improves the setting with? It doesn't really seems like it does much aside reproducing anti-Chinese sentiment in the US (not necessarily assuming the US side, though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}